  "note": "Complete save_point_cloud CSV function: path/parent handling, actual UTF-8 text-file open, canonical XYZ header, unchanged Python float formatting via csv.writer, all data writes, internal cleanup and close/flush. No fsync durability guarantee. Source loading, imports, fingerprints, output hashing/validation and removal are excluded. Candidate copies full XYZ into a stable numeric snapshot and materializes at most 65536 Python rows per batch; old writer materializes all Python rows. Entire existing measured compared subsets are used, without further thinning, generated coordinates or perturbation; not independent surveys. Excluded full-byte parity pair, first pair and one warm-up pair precede five default alternating timed pairs. Every save is hashed, both parity files are retained and checked byte-for-byte; all baseline parity CSV coordinates round-trip bitwise to the full oracle. Other outputs are removed outside timing. Fresh process per source/pass, warm pages. No peak RSS, cold CLI, complete conversion, other-format, parallel or GPU speed claim."
